<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siegfried, Count of Luxembourg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 922–998</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siegfried (c. 922–998) was a Lotharingian count regarded as the founder of Luxembourg. In 963 he acquired the rocky promontory of Lucilinburhuc above the Alzette from St Maximin's Abbey at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a> and built a castle there, around which the city of Luxembourg grew. His descendants included the counts of Luxembourg, and his daughter Cunigunde married Emperor Henry II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siegfried-count-of-luxembourg.jpg" alt="Siegfried, Count of Luxembourg" width="297" height="297" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown - uploaded by user Otets · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Siegfried_I_of_Luxembourg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
